docs {
  # HANDYMAN — Mobile App API

  One Flutter app, one account, two roles. Everyone signs up as a client;
  "become a master" adds a master profile on top of the same account. There is
  a **single** Sanctum token (`{{token}}`) — it opens the client endpoints
  immediately and the master endpoints once an administrator has approved the
  application and issued a subscription.

  ## Run order (fresh database)

  1. `01_auth` → Request OTP, then put the received code into the `otp` env
     variable and run Verify OTP — it saves `{{token}}`. When the response says
     `delivery: "manual"` no gateway phone was connected and the code is in
     `storage/logs/laravel.log` / the admin panel instead of an SMS.
  2. `01_auth` → Complete Registration — name + city are required before ordering.
  3. `04_orders` → Create Order — saves `{{order_id}}`.
  4. `05_become_master` → Submit Application — status becomes `pending`.
  5. Admin panel → **Заявки мастеров** → approve + issue a subscription.
  6. `06_master_profile` → Get My Profile — the same token now passes `ensure.master`.
  7. `06_master_profile` → Send Location, then `07_master_orders` → Available
     Orders (or By Category for every order in the master's trades), then
     Respond — the master offers himself, the order stays `pending`.
  8. `04_orders` → List Order Responses (saves `{{response_id}}`), then Approve
     Response — the order becomes `assigned` and starts answering in
     `10_realtime` → Order Track.
  9. Renewal: `08_master_subscription` → Submit Subscription Request, then
     Admin panel → **Заявки на тариф** → approve — the running subscription's
     `expires_at` (and `access_expires_at`) moves forward by the plan's days at
     once; it stays a single subscription, nothing is queued.

  For pushes, register the phone's FCM token once after sign-in:
  `11_push` → Register Device.

  ## Folders

  | Folder                 | Token needed | Notes                                  |
  |------------------------|--------------|----------------------------------------|
  | `01_auth`              | partly       | OTP is public, the rest needs a token  |
  | `02_catalog`           | no           | public catalog                         |
  | `03_profile`           | yes          | client profile                         |
  | `04_orders`            | yes          | client orders + master responses        |
  | `05_become_master`     | yes          | application + review status            |
  | `06_master_profile`    | yes, approved| profile, availability, GPS             |
  | `07_master_orders`     | yes, approved| feeds (radius / category), work, tasks |
  | `08_master_subscription`| partly      | price list public; own subscription, plan requests (any client) |
  | `09_settings`          | no           | one T&C text, shared by both roles     |
  | `10_realtime`          | yes          | Reverb channel auth + master trail     |
  | `11_push`              | yes          | FCM device tokens for push notifications |

  ## Why the master endpoints may answer 403

  Every rejection carries a machine-readable `reason` so the app can route to
  the right screen instead of guessing from the message.

  | `reason`               | Meaning                                        |
  |------------------------|------------------------------------------------|
  | `token_required`       | Not a client token at all                      |
  | `not_a_master`         | Never applied — show "become a master"         |
  | `application_pending`  | Waiting for the administrator                  |
  | `application_rejected` | Rejected — `rejection_reason` explains why     |
  | `disabled`             | Blocked by the administrator                   |
  | `access_expired`       | Subscription ran out — show the renewal screen |

  ## Push notifications

  Delivered through FCM to every phone registered with `11_push` → Register
  Device. Title and body arrive translated (language remembered at
  registration). `data` always carries `type` (table below) and `audience`
  (`client` / `master` — which half of the app to open). All `data` values are
  **strings** (FCM requirement).

  | `type`                          | `audience` | When                                          | Extra `data`                                  |
  |---------------------------------|------------|-----------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|
  | `order.response.created`        | client     | a master responded to the order               | `order_id`, `response_id`                     |
  | `master.assigned`               | client     | a master was assigned to the order            | `order_id`                                    |
  | `order.status.changed`          | client     | order started / completed                     | `order_id`, `status`                          |
  | `order.nearby`                  | master     | a new order reached the master's radius       | `order_id`                                    |
  | `order.response.approved`       | master     | the client picked this master                 | `order_id`                                    |
  | `order.cancelled`               | master     | the master's order was cancelled              | `order_id`                                    |
  | `subscription.expiring`         | master     | ends within 24 h, not renewed yet             | `subscription_id`, `expires_at` (ISO)         |
  | `subscription.expired`          | master     | ran out, access closed                        | `subscription_id`                             |
  | `subscription_request.approved` | master     | plan request approved, access extended        | `subscription_request_id`, `subscription_id`  |
  | `subscription_request.rejected` | master     | plan request rejected; body = reason, if any  | `subscription_request_id`                     |

  ## Localization

  Every request sends `X-Locale: {{locale}}`. Flip the `locale` env variable
  between `tk` and `ru` to check translated names and error messages.
}
